}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "Yes \[LongDash] the immediate problem is simple: your new definition is\n\
\n```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diag_, antiParticleRules_Association] := ...\n```\n\
\nbut you called it as\n\n```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diags[[1]]]\n```\n\nwith \
only one argument. Because of that, ``diagramAmplitude`` never evaluated, so \
``processed`` never became an association, and then things like \
``processed[\"VertexStructures\"]`` remained symbolic, producing the \
``Values::invrl`` cascade.\n\n## Immediate fix\n\nEither call it with the \
second argument:\n\n```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diags[[1]], \
antiParticleRulesFromModel[sm]]\n```\n\nor define a one-argument wrapper:\n\n\
```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diag_] := diagramAmplitude[diag, \
antiParticleRulesFromModel[sm]]\n```\n\n---\n\n## But there is also a \
structural issue\n\nYour current ``spinorVarianceAtEndpoint`` logic can\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t really distinguish particle end vs antiparticle end \
robustly just from\n\n```wl\nLookup[antiParticleRules, endpointParticle] === \
oppositeParticle\n```\n\nbecause for a pair like ``\"e\"`` and ``\"E\"``, \
both directions are true in the inverse sense. What you really want is \
simpler:\n\n* for each internal edge, pick the propagating particle from \
``diag[\"Propagators\"][edge, \"Particle\"]``\n* at the endpoint where \
``diag[\"InternalEdgeLabels\"][edge][vertex]`` equals that particle, use \
``\"Upper\"``\n* at the other endpoint, use ``\"Lower\"``\n\nThat directly \
matches your statement:\n* particle end \\(\\to\\) upper\n* antiparticle end \
\\(\\to\\) lower\n\n---\n\n## Cleaner corrected version\n\nReplace your \
spin-index code with this:\n\n```wl\nClearAll[\n\t  spinorVarianceAtEndpoint,\
\n\t  symmetrizeIndices,\n\t  edgeSpinMultiplicity,\n\t  edgeSpinIndexData,\n\
\t  makeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit,\n\t  makeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit,\n\t  \
diagramAmplitude\n\t]\n\nspinorVarianceAtEndpoint[diag_, edge_, vertex_] := \
Module[\n\t  {propParticle, endpointParticle},\n\t  \n\t  propParticle = \
diag[\"Propagators\"][edge, \"Particle\"];\n\t  endpointParticle = \
diag[\"InternalEdgeLabels\"][edge][vertex];\n\t  \n\t  If[endpointParticle \
=== propParticle, \"Upper\", \"Lower\"]\n\t]\n\nsymmetrizeIndices[expr_, \
inds_List] := Module[\n\t  {perms},\n\t  perms = Permutations[inds];\n\t  \
Total[(expr /. Thread[inds -> #]) & /@ perms] / Length[perms]\n\t]\n\n\
edgeSpinMultiplicity[diag_, edge_] := Module[\n\t  {vertices},\n\t  \n\t  \
vertices = Keys[diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"][edge]];\n\t  \n\t  Max[\n\t    \
Cases[\n\t      vertices,\n\t      vertex_ :> Count[\n\t        Cases[\n\t    \
      Lookup[Last[diag[\"VertexStructures\"][vertex]], \"Expression\", 1],\n\t\
          Spinor[\"Spin\", _, diag[\"InternalEdgeIndices\"][edge][vertex]],\n\
\t          Infinity\n\t        ],\n\t        _\n\t      ]\n\t    ]\n\t  ]\n\t\
]\n\nedgeSpinIndexData[diag_] := Module[\n\t  {edges, multiplicities, \
starts},\n\t  \n\t  edges = Keys[diag[\"InternalEdgeLabels\"]];\n\t  \
multiplicities = edgeSpinMultiplicity[diag, #] & /@ edges;\n\t  starts = Most \
@ FoldList[Plus, 1, multiplicities];\n\t  \n\t  AssociationThread[\n\t    \
edges,\n\t    MapThread[\n\t      Array[Symbol[\"i\" <> ToString[#]] &, #1, \
#2] &,\n\t      {multiplicities, starts}\n\t    ]\n\t  ]\n\t]\n\n\
makeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit[\n\t  vertexStructure_Association,\n\t  \
vertex_,\n\t  diag_,\n\t  edgeIndexData_Association\n\t] := Module[\n\t  {\n\t\
    expr, incidentLegs, spinorData, grouped, replacementRules, newExpr\n\t  \
},\n\t  \n\t  expr = vertexStructure[\"Expression\"];\n\t  incidentLegs = \
diag[\"IncidentLegData\"][vertex];\n\t  \n\t  spinorData = Cases[\n\t    \
expr,\n\t    s : Spinor[\"Spin\", sa_, mp_Multiparticle] :> Module[\n\t      \
{leg},\n\t      \n\t      leg = SelectFirst[\n\t        incidentLegs,\n\t     \
   #[\"Kind\"] === \"Internal\" && #[\"Index\"] === mp &\n\t      ];\n\t      \
\n\t      If[MissingQ[leg],\n\t        Nothing,\n\t        <|\n\t          \
\"Spinor\" -> s,\n\t          \"SpinType\" -> sa,\n\t          \
\"Multiparticle\" -> mp,\n\t          \"Edge\" -> leg[\"Source\"]\n\t        \
|>\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    Infinity\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  If[spinorData === \
{}, Return[vertexStructure]];\n\t  \n\t  grouped = GroupBy[spinorData, #Edge \
&];\n\t  \n\t  replacementRules = Flatten @ KeyValueMap[\n\t    \
Function[{edge, items},\n\t      Module[\n\t        {inds, variance},\n\t     \
   \n\t        inds = edgeIndexData[edge];\n\t        variance = \
spinorVarianceAtEndpoint[diag, edge, vertex];\n\t        \n\t        \
MapThread[\n\t          #1[\"Spinor\"] :> Spinor[\"Spin\", variance, \
#1[\"SpinType\"], #1[\"Multiparticle\"], #2] &,\n\t          {items, inds}\n\t\
        ]\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    grouped\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  newExpr = \
expr /. replacementRules;\n\t  \n\t  newExpr = Fold[\n\t    \
Function[{currentExpr, edge},\n\t      If[Length[grouped[edge]] > 1,\n\t      \
  symmetrizeIndices[currentExpr, Take[edgeIndexData[edge], \
Length[grouped[edge]]]],\n\t        currentExpr\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    \
newExpr,\n\t    Keys[grouped]\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  Join[vertexStructure, \
<|\"Expression\" -> newExpr|>]\n\t]\n\nmakeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit[diag_] \
:= Module[\n\t  {edgeIndexData, newVertexStructures},\n\t  \n\t  \
edgeIndexData = edgeSpinIndexData[diag];\n\t  \n\t  newVertexStructures = \
Association @ KeyValueMap[\n\t    Function[{vertex, structures},\n\t      \
vertex -> Replace[\n\t        structures,\n\t        {\n\t          {} :> {},\
\n\t          list_List :> ReplacePart[\n\t            list,\n\t            \
-1 -> makeVertexSpinIndicesExplicit[Last[list], vertex, diag, edgeIndexData]\n\
\t          ]\n\t        }\n\t      ]\n\t    ],\n\t    \
diag[\"VertexStructures\"]\n\t  ];\n\t  \n\t  Join[\n\t    diag,\n\t    <|\n\t\
      \"VertexStructures\" -> newVertexStructures,\n\t      \"SpinIndices\" \
-> edgeIndexData\n\t    |>\n\t  ]\n\t]\n\ndiagramAmplitude[diag_] := Module[\n\
\t  {processed, vertexFactors, propagatorFactors},\n\t  \n\t  processed = \
makeDiagramSpinIndicesExplicit[diag];\n\t  \n\t  vertexFactors = Replace[\n\t \
   Values[processed[\"VertexStructures\"]],\n\t    {\n\t      {} :> 1,\n\t    \
  list_List :> Lookup[Last[list], \"Expression\", 1]\n\t    },\n\t    1\n\t  \
];\n\t  \n\t  propagatorFactors = Lookup[Values[processed[\"Propagators\"]], \
\"Factor\", 1];\n\t  \n\t  Times @@ Join[vertexFactors, propagatorFactors] / \
I\n\t]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why this version is better\n\nIt fixes two things:\n\
\n### 1. Correct evaluation path\n``diagramAmplitude`` is again a \
one-argument function, so your call\n\n```wl\ndiagramAmplitude[diags[[1]]]\n\
```\n\nworks.\n\n### 2. Matching indices across propagator ends\nEach \
internal edge gets its own index set via ``edgeSpinIndexData[diag]``.  \nSo \
if edge ``e`` gets ``{i1}``, then both endpoint spinors on that edge use that \
same ``i1``.\n\n### 3. Correct upper/lower assignment\nThis is now determined \
by the propagator\[CloseCurlyQuote]s chosen particle identity:\n\n```wl\n\
If[endpointParticle === propParticle, \"Upper\", \"Lower\"]\n```\n\nSo the \
propagator particle end gets upper, the antiparticle end gets lower.\n\n---\n\
\n## Expected behavior\n\nIf one endpoint has something like\n\n```wl\n\
Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", Multiparticle[2,4,5]]\n```\n\nand that endpoint \
is the particle end of the propagator, it becomes\n\n```wl\nSpinor[\"Spin\", \
\"Upper\", \"Angle\", Multiparticle[2,4,5], i1]\n```\n\nwhile the other \
endpoint becomes\n\n```wl\nSpinor[\"Spin\", \"Lower\", \"Angle\", \
Multiparticle[2,4,5], i1]\n```\n\nusing the same ``i1``.\n\nIf there are two \
such spinors on the same endpoint for the same ``Multiparticle[...]``, they \
get something like ``i1``, ``i2`` and the vertex expression is symmetrized in \
those indices.\n\n---\n\n## Try this now\n\n```wl\n\
diagramAmplitude[diags[[1]]]\n```\n\nIf you want, next I can help you make \
the amplitude function also return:\n* the separate vertex product,\n* the \
separate propagator product,\n* and the full product,\n\nso debugging the \
symbolic structure is easier.", "ChatData" -> 
