 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "Yes \[LongDash] that is the right fix.\n\nRather than re-deriving \
particle vs antiparticle during amplitude construction, you should store that \
information explicitly in the diagram when you build the internal edge \
labels. Then the amplitude code becomes simple and reliable.\n\n## Best \
approach\n\nAugment each internal edge in the diagram with metadata like:\n\n\
* which endpoint is the **particle** end\n* which endpoint is the \
**antiparticle** end\n* what the particle name is\n* what the antiparticle \
name is\n\nThen later the spinor-index code can just ask:\n\n* is this vertex \
the particle end? $$\\to$$ use ``\"Upper\"``\n* is this vertex the \
antiparticle end? $$\\to$$ use ``\"Lower\"``\n\nThat is much better than \
inferring it afterwards.\n\n---\n\n## Suggested change: enrich propagator \
data\n\nRight now your ``internalPropagatorData`` stores something like:\n\n\
```wl\n<|\n  edge -> <|\n    \"Particle\" -> particle,\n    \"Index\" -> \
index,\n    \"Mass\" -> mass,\n    \"Factor\" -> ...\n  |>\n|>\n```\n\nModify \
it so it also stores endpoint orientation information from \
``internalEdgeLabels``:\n\n```wl\ninternalPropagatorData[\n\t  graph_, \n\t  \
internalEdgeLabels_Association, \n\t  internalEdgeIndices_Association, \n\t  \
particleMassRules_Association\n\t] := Association @ KeyValueMap[\n\t  \
Function[{edge, endpointParticleLabels}, \n\t    Module[\n\t      {\n\t       \
 particle, antiParticle, index, mass, particleVertex, antiParticleVertex\n\t  \
    }, \n\t      \n\t      particle = First[Values[endpointParticleLabels]];\n\
\t      antiParticle = Last[Values[endpointParticleLabels]];\n\t      index = \
First[Values[internalEdgeIndices[edge]]];\n\t      mass = \
Lookup[particleMassRules, particle, Missing[\"MassNotFound\"]];\n\t      \n\t \
     particleVertex = FirstCase[\n\t        Keys[endpointParticleLabels], \n\t\
        v_ /; endpointParticleLabels[v] === particle\n\t      ];\n\t      \n\t\
      antiParticleVertex = FirstCase[\n\t        \
Keys[endpointParticleLabels], \n\t        v_ /; v =!= particleVertex\n\t      \
];\n\t      \n\t      edge -> <|\n\t        \"Particle\" -> particle, \n\t    \
    \"Antiparticle\" -> antiParticle, \n\t        \"ParticleVertex\" -> \
particleVertex, \n\t        \"AntiparticleVertex\" -> antiParticleVertex, \n\t\
        \"Index\" -> index, \n\t        \"Mass\" -> mass, \n\t        \
\"Factor\" -> If[\n\t          MissingQ[mass], \n\t          \
Missing[\"MassNotFound\", particle], \n\t          I / PropDen[Mom[index], \
mass]\n\t        ]\n\t      |>\n\t    ]\n\t  ], \n\t  internalEdgeLabels\n\t]\
\n```\n\nBut this version is still slightly unsafe because \
``First[Values[...]]`` depends on association ordering.\n\nSo better is to \
explicitly derive particle/antiparticle using the model relation.\n\n---\n\n\
## Better: create particle-antiparticle tags when assigning internal edges\n\n\
Your ``internalEdgeAssignments`` currently builds:\n\n```wl\n<|edge -> <|u -> \
particle, v -> anti|>|>\n```\n\nThat is exactly where the orientation is \
known. So instead of storing only endpoint labels, store richer endpoint data \
there.\n\nFor example:\n\n```wl\ninternalEdgeAssignments[\n\t  \
internalEdges_List, \n\t  particleTypes_List, \n\t  \
antiParticleRules_Association\n\t] := Module[\n\t  {choicesPerEdge}, \n\t  \n\
\t  choicesPerEdge = Function[edge, \n\t    DeleteDuplicates @ Flatten[\n\t   \
   Table[\n\t        With[{anti = Lookup[antiParticleRules, particle, \
Missing[\"NotFound\"]]}, \n\t          If[\n\t            MissingQ[anti], \n\t\
            {}, \n\t            With[{ends = Sort[List @@ edge]}, \n\t        \
      {\n\t                <|\n\t                  \"EndpointLabels\" -> \
AssociationThread[ends, {particle, anti}], \n\t                  \"Particle\" \
-> particle, \n\t                  \"Antiparticle\" -> anti, \n\t             \
     \"ParticleVertex\" -> ends[[1]], \n\t                  \
\"AntiparticleVertex\" -> ends[[2]]\n\t                |>, \n\t               \
 <|\n\t                  \"EndpointLabels\" -> AssociationThread[ends, {anti, \
particle}], \n\t                  \"Particle\" -> particle, \n\t              \
    \"Antiparticle\" -> anti, \n\t                  \"ParticleVertex\" -> \
ends[[2]], \n\t                  \"AntiparticleVertex\" -> ends[[1]]\n\t      \
          |>\n\t              }\n\t            ]\n\t          ]\n\t        ], \
\n\t        {particle, particleTypes}\n\t      ], \n\t      1\n\t    ]\n\t  ] \
/@ internalEdges;\n\t  \n\t  AssociationThread[internalEdges, #] & /@ \
Tuples[choicesPerEdge]\n\t]\n```\n\nThen each edge assignment contains all \
the information you need.\n\n---\n\n## Then adjust diagram construction\n\nIn \
``decorateTopology``, instead of storing only:\n\n```wl\n\"InternalEdgeLabels\
\" -> internalEdgeLabels\n```\n\nstore both:\n\n```wl\n\"InternalEdgeData\" \
-> internalEdgeData,\n\"InternalEdgeLabels\" -> \
AssociationMap[internalEdgeData[#,\"EndpointLabels\"] &, \
Keys[internalEdgeData]]\n```\n\nor just derive ``InternalEdgeLabels`` from \
``InternalEdgeData`` for backward compatibility.\n\nFor example inside \
``decorateTopology``:\n\n```wl\nFlatten @ Table[\n\t  Module[{edgeLabels}, \n\
\t    edgeLabels = AssociationMap[\n\t      \
internalEdgeData[#,\"EndpointLabels\"] &, \n\t      Keys[internalEdgeData]\n\t\
    ];\n\t    \n\t    If[\n\t      validVertexAssignmentFastQ[\n\t        \
graph, \n\t        internalVerts, \n\t        extMap, \n\t        edgeLabels, \
\n\t        model\n\t      ], \n\t      <|\n\t        \"Graph\" -> graph, \n\t\
        \"ExternalAssignment\" -> extMap, \n\t        \"InternalEdgeData\" -> \
internalEdgeData, \n\t        \"InternalEdgeLabels\" -> edgeLabels, \n\t      \
  \"InternalVertices\" -> internalVerts, \n\t        \"LeafVertices\" -> \
leafVerts\n\t      |>, \n\t      Nothing\n\t    ]\n\t  ], \n\t  {extMap, \
extAssignments}, \n\t  {internalEdgeData, edgeAssignments}\n\t]\n```\n\n---\n\
\n## Then amplitude construction becomes trivial\n\nNow define \
particle/antiparticle end lookup by using ``InternalEdgeData``:\n\n```wl\n\
spinorVarianceAtEndpoint[diag_, edge_, vertex_] := Module[\n\t  {edgeData}, \n\
\t  \n\t  edgeData = diag[\"InternalEdgeData\"][edge];\n\t  \n\t  Which[\n\t  \
  vertex === edgeData[\"ParticleVertex\"], \"Upper\", \n\t    vertex === \
edgeData[\"AntiparticleVertex\"], \"Lower\", \n\t    True, \
Missing[\"InvalidVertex\"]\n\t  ]\n\t]\n```\n\nThat is robust and completely \
avoids guessing.\n\n---\n\n## Strongly recommended minimal retrofit\n\nIf you \
do not want to rewrite too much, the smallest good change is:\n\n### 1. After \
creating ``internalEdgeLabels``, create an additional association:\n\n```wl\n\
internalEdgeOrientationData[\n\t  internalEdgeLabels_Association, \n\t  \
antiParticleRules_Association\n\t] := Association @ KeyValueMap[\n\t  \
Function[{edge, labels}, \n\t    Module[{u, v, pu, pv}, \n\t      {u, v} = \
List @@ edge;\n\t      pu = labels[u];\n\t      pv = labels[v];\n\t      \n\t \
     edge -> Which[\n\t        Lookup[antiParticleRules, pu, None] === pv, \n\
\t        <|\n\t          \"Particle\" -> pu, \n\t          \"Antiparticle\" \
-> pv, \n\t          \"ParticleVertex\" -> u, \n\t          \
\"AntiparticleVertex\" -> v\n\t        |>, \n\t        \n\t        \
Lookup[antiParticleRules, pv, None] === pu, \n\t        <|\n\t          \
\"Particle\" -> pv, \n\t          \"Antiparticle\" -> pu, \n\t          \
\"ParticleVertex\" -> v, \n\t          \"AntiparticleVertex\" -> u\n\t        \
|>, \n\t        \n\t        True, \n\t        <|\n\t          \"Particle\" -> \
pu, \n\t          \"Antiparticle\" -> pv, \n\t          \"ParticleVertex\" -> \
u, \n\t          \"AntiparticleVertex\" -> v, \n\t          \"Warning\" -> \
\"CouldNotVerifyParticleAntiparticleOrientation\"\n\t        |>\n\t      ]\n\t\
    ]\n\t  ], \n\t  internalEdgeLabels\n\t]\n```\n\n### 2. Store it in the \
diagram:\n\ninside ``decorateTopology`` add:\n\n```wl\nedgeOrientation = \
internalEdgeOrientationData[internalEdgeLabels, antiParticleRules];\n```\n\n\
and store\n\n```wl\n\"InternalEdgeOrientation\" -> edgeOrientation\n```\n\n\
### 3. Use that in amplitude building:\n\n```wl\n\
spinorVarianceAtEndpoint[diag_, edge_, vertex_] := Which[\n\t  vertex === \
diag[\"InternalEdgeOrientation\"][edge, \"ParticleVertex\"], \"Upper\", \n\t  \
vertex === diag[\"InternalEdgeOrientation\"][edge, \"AntiparticleVertex\"], \
\"Lower\", \n\t  True, Missing[\"InvalidVertex\"]\n\t]\n```\n\n---\n\n## My \
recommendation\n\nI would use this **minimal retrofit** first, because it \
requires the fewest code changes and fits your existing structure.\n\nIf you \
want, I can now write the exact replacement definitions for:\n\n* \
``internalEdgeAssignments``\n* ``decorateTopology``\n* \
``internalPropagatorData``\n* ``spinorVarianceAtEndpoint``\n\nusing your \
current codebase style, so you can paste them in directly.", "ChatData" -> 
